s, calculate percentage parts, and solve discount, GST and annual simple-interest problems with stated rates.","topic_order":6},{"id":"2c9cb8ea-145c-4dc3-8b85-106b4a55c15c","name":"Rate","level_id":"1a6f0236-7e83-493d-9bca-d7d21f232c1a","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:29:07.840959+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Understand quantities per unit and calculate a rate, total amount or number of units.","topic_order":7},{"id":"13d391aa-7de4-47fb-b812-8c1b8dcb3347","name":"Area of Triangles and Composite Figures","level_id":"1a6f0236-7e83-493d-9bca-d7d21f232c1a","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:29:07.840959+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Identify base and perpendicular height, calculate triangle area and calculate areas of non-overlapping composite figures.","topic_order":8},{"id":"4a52c7d4-eb52-4a3e-a983-3ba4f2ffaf9a","name":"Volume of Cubes and Cuboids","level_id":"1a6f0236-7e83-493d-9bca-d7d21f232c1a","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:29:07.840959+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Build solids from unit cubes; recognise cubic units and isometric representations; find cuboid and cube volume and related liquid measures.","topic_order":9},{"id":"05eae934-1e40-4204-a105-68319c005597","name":"Angle Relationships","level_id":"1a6f0236-7e83-493d-9bca-d7d21f232c1a","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:29:07.840959+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Recognise angles on a straight line, at a point and vertically opposite angles and use their relationships to find unknown angles.","topic_order":10},{"id":"0065f434-d293-4936-bfdc-1fbae7d8c85d","name":"Triangle Properties and Unknown Angles","level_id":"1a6f0236-7e83-493d-9bca-d7d21f232c1a","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:29:07.840959+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Recognise isosceles, equilateral and right-angled triangles and use the triangle angle sum to solve unknown angles.","topic_order":11},{"id":"72b53116-6e9a-42af-8768-931f2785f3f2","name":"Parallelograms, Rhombuses and Trapeziums","level_id":"1a6f0236-7e83-493d-9bca-d7d21f232c1a","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:29:07.840959+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Recognise properties of special quadrilaterals and use given angle facts to solve unknown angles.","topic_order":12},{"id":"4ba9548c-430b-4a6a-9060-b43165aad84c","name":"Division of Fractions","level_id":"95912ac2-bfe1-4e24-845b-1b9749b645d4","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:59:16.001065+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Divide proper fractions by whole numbers, and divide whole numbers or proper fractions by proper fractions without a calculator.","topic_order":1},{"id":"bb15ed93-d75f-4ecc-a16e-adfcf20320d1","name":"Reverse Percentages and Percentage Change","level_id":"95912ac2-bfe1-4e24-845b-1b9749b645d4","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:59:16.001065+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Find a whole from its percentage part and calculate percentage increase or decrease.","topic_order":2},{"id":"27118cb2-0e53-4d1d-a6bb-c7a52e7ee79b","name":"Ratios and Equivalent Ratios","level_id":"95912ac2-bfe1-4e24-845b-1b9749b645d4","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:59:16.001065+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Interpret two-part and three-part whole-number ratios and identify, simplify and compare equivalent ratios.","topic_order":3},{"id":"131cff26-924f-4564-97ab-b80f3036713b","name":"Sharing in a Ratio and Fraction Relationships","level_id":"95912ac2-bfe1-4e24-845b-1b9749b645d4","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:59:16.001065+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Divide quantities into two or three whole-number ratio parts, solve equivalent-ratio missing values and connect ratios with fractions.","topic_order":4},{"id":"24c57c88-8b4f-4a7e-80b3-c33f1d9f030a","name":"Algebraic Expressions","level_id":"95912ac2-bfe1-4e24-845b-1b9749b645d4","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:59:16.001065+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Represent unknown numbers using letters, write simple algebraic expressions, and simplify linear expressions without brackets.","topic_order":5},{"id":"5b99e707-682d-45be-948f-341f57c880c7","name":"Substitution and Linear Equations","level_id":"95912ac2-bfe1-4e24-845b-1b9749b645d4","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:59:16.001065+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Evaluate simple algebraic expressions and solve simple linear equations with whole-number coefficients.","topic_order":6},{"id":"5b07b062-6a15-46c7-92c3-3802e45ed2e4","name":"Area and Circumference of Circles","level_id":"95912ac2-bfe1-4e24-845b-1b9749b645d4","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:59:16.001065+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Find a circle’s circumference and area using the specified value of pi.","topic_order":7},{"id":"2afc72ff-4343-49c2-9d50-de62d38ad66a","name":"Semicircles, Quarter Circles and Composite Figures","level_id":"95912ac2-bfe1-4e24-845b-1b9749b645d4","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:59:16.001065+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Calculate areas and complete perimeters of semicircles, quarter circles and specified composite figures.","topic_order":8},{"id":"51c85230-bd7a-4d99-ade2-51451df1ce3a","name":"Cuboid Volume, Missing Dimensions and Roots","level_id":"95912ac2-bfe1-4e24-845b-1b9749b645d4","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:59:16.001065+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Find unknown cuboid dimensions, cube edges, face areas and use square and cube roots as stated in Primary 6.","topic_order":9},{"id":"7f01b3ce-1427-4eec-b753-1cf88c66d671","name":"Unknown Angles in Special Quadrilaterals","level_id":"95912ac2-bfe1-4e24-845b-1b9749b645d4","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:59:16.001065+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Solve unknown angles in explicitly described composite figures involving squares, rectangles, triangles, parallelograms, rhombuses and trapeziums, without adding construction lines.","topic_order":10},{"id":"56dfa685-f3c3-4784-b8a6-735254836e47","name":"Average of a Set of Data","level_id":"95912ac2-bfe1-4e24-845b-1b9749b645d4","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:59:16.001065+00:00","subject_id":"b1c22f4e-87b6-4026-b0b0-e2a8d41f34dc","description":"Find averages, totals and number of observations using the total-and-count relationship.","topic_order":11}]$curriculum$::jsonb) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.topic_learning_goals SELECT * FROM jsonb_populate_recordset(NULL::public.topic_learning_goals, $curriculum$[{"id":"83f2e3a3-6a4b-4a1f-b6b3-26a07ba45eb5","topic_id":"bba3ee86-82bb-43d9-a4da-4ac736c4c1aa","goal_text":"identify and explain the characteristics of living things.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"moe primary science syllabus 2023, page 38"},{"id":"7d672a4e-dcba-4ae9-83a8-c42a37c3e354","topic_id":"bba3ee86-82bb-43d9-a4da-4ac736c4c1aa","goal_text":"distinguish living things from non-living things using evidence.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"moe primary science syllabus 2023, page 38"},{"id":"ebbec800-b6f6-4bf6-8385-e5cc186b3995","topic_id":"bba3ee86-82bb-43d9-a4da-4ac736c4c1aa","goal_text":"recognise the major groups of living things: plants, animals, fungi and bacteria.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"moe primary science syllabus 2023, page 38"},{"id":"65b55dc9-61cd-4799-a3b1-522efcabda6a","topic_id":"bba3ee86-82bb-43d9-a4da-4ac736c4c1aa","goal_text":"identify broad subgroups of plants and animals.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"moe primary science syllabus 2023, page 38"},{"id":"afab5304-c677-472d-b81d-bd6de604c885","topic_id":"bba3ee86-82bb-43d9-a4da-4ac736c4c1aa","goal_text":"classify living things using common observable characteristics.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"moe primary science syllabus 2023, page 38"},{"id":"81507539-0a85-4e86-a2b5-09118cf441ca","topic_id":"d7263e39-a997-4b23-9797-75dc75cc1f75","goal_text":"Identify common materials such as wood, metal, ceramic, rubber, glass, plastic and fabric.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Diversity of Materials"},{"id":"5e9c7db9-14ed-4e0d-a212-3bafd2c133b1","topic_id":"d7263e39-a997-4b23-9797-75dc75cc1f75","goal_text":"Compare the strength and flexibility of materials.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Diversity of Materials"},{"id":"87859852-5b0b-4fb9-b17a-3940abe5564d","topic_id":"d7263e39-a997-4b23-9797-75dc75cc1f75","goal_text":"Investigate whether different objects float or sink in water.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Diversity of Materials"},{"id":"6eb3c70f-4b8a-4003-80dc-5ace9e84fa5f","topic_id":"d7263e39-a997-4b23-9797-75dc75cc1f75","goal_text":"Compare materials according to whether they absorb water.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Diversity of Materials"},{"id":"1f02d8a1-b2d5-41db-bfbc-f66043e8ebf7","topic_id":"d7263e39-a997-4b23-9797-75dc75cc1f75","goal_text":"Compare how much light passes through materials and explain suitable everyday uses.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Diversity of Materials"},{"id":"9ef45b78-e971-4bef-9e73-73ae0fd3a1ea","topic_id":"762e6037-425b-44cf-8aeb-6a087efa46cc","goal_text":"Recognise that living things have life cycles and that the patterns repeat.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Life Cycles"},{"id":"6ac811d8-9bec-4479-bbee-caf1a8cc2a70","topic_id":"762e6037-425b-44cf-8aeb-6a087efa46cc","goal_text":"Observe the life-cycle stages of flowering plants grown from seeds.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Life Cycles"},{"id":"3e3f1135-0011-4998-9086-cd71aa029fd4","topic_id":"762e6037-425b-44cf-8aeb-6a087efa46cc","goal_text":"Describe and compare the life cycles of chickens and frogs.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Life Cycles"},{"id":"ce0bbb69-333d-4602-bd06-e869753ad8b6","topic_id":"762e6037-425b-44cf-8aeb-6a087efa46cc","goal_text":"Compare the life cycles of cockroaches, grasshoppers, beetles, butterflies and mosquitoes.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Life Cycles"},{"id":"6b7b54bd-57ac-4e51-bd91-de57ebee77b7","topic_id":"762e6037-425b-44cf-8aeb-6a087efa46cc","goal_text":"Record life-cycle observations and show care towards plants and animals.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Life Cycles"},{"id":"59bd5e39-6ad3-444d-a5b6-25c639698979","topic_id":"be638cf3-40a0-48ae-89c1-f20a1e63d137","goal_text":"Recognise that magnetic forces can push or pull without direct contact.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Interaction of Forces (Magnets)"},{"id":"88d1cc21-e8d6-469b-a695-3212826bc49a","topic_id":"be638cf3-40a0-48ae-89c1-f20a1e63d137","goal_text":"Distinguish magnets, magnetic materials and non-magnetic materials.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Interaction of Forces (Magnets)"},{"id":"346d8099-8b8c-4b6b-b197-4f9646dee1c7","topic_id":"be638cf3-40a0-48ae-89c1-f20a1e63d137","goal_text":"Identify the two poles of a magnet and the North-South direction of a freely suspended bar magnet.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Interaction of Forces (Magnets)"},{"id":"b09e89b9-35f4-4b8e-9f12-536424e20a24","topic_id":"be638cf3-40a0-48ae-89c1-f20a1e63d137","goal_text":"Predict attraction and repulsion between like and unlike magnetic poles.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Interaction of Forces (Magnets)"},{"id":"9d89cf7c-4e45-4378-be1b-850adbbce2fd","topic_id":"be638cf3-40a0-48ae-89c1-f20a1e63d137","goal_text":"Describe how to make a magnet using the stroke method.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Interaction of Forces (Magnets)"},{"id":"d9ab4900-3270-4334-8b2f-8604b6a116c0","topic_id":"be638cf3-40a0-48ae-89c1-f20a1e63d137","goal_text":"Describe how to make an electromagnet using the electrical method.","goal_order":6,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Interaction of Forces (Magnets)"},{"id":"1890bcca-5e1d-4076-953f-803b62a09dce","topic_id":"be638cf3-40a0-48ae-89c1-f20a1e63d137","goal_text":"Recognise everyday uses of magnets and explain their usefulness.","goal_order":7,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P3 Interaction of Forces (Magnets)"},{"id":"affc3287-edc1-4f69-bdd2-33d34ae42726","topic_id":"192d0ece-5762-4458-ba4b-2bcd0e8b406d","goal_text":"Identify roots, stems and leaves on common plants.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Plant System (Plant Parts and Functions)"},{"id":"2591eb99-f44f-4ccc-876e-330fcdb14d11","topic_id":"192d0ece-5762-4458-ba4b-2bcd0e8b406d","goal_text":"Explain how roots anchor plants and take in water and mineral salts.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Plant System (Plant Parts and Functions)"},{"id":"ec8a60c2-3b7c-480c-a59a-2c7bfabf4197","topic_id":"192d0ece-5762-4458-ba4b-2bcd0e8b406d","goal_text":"Explain how stems hold up leaves and other parts of a plant.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Plant System (Plant Parts and Functions)"},{"id":"6f2324d2-63c1-40b6-85a6-c55c0458287d","topic_id":"192d0ece-5762-4458-ba4b-2bcd0e8b406d","goal_text":"Describe how leaves make food for the plant.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Plant System (Plant Parts and Functions)"},{"id":"0abde32b-13e1-4806-8ed6-6769282ed37f","topic_id":"192d0ece-5762-4458-ba4b-2bcd0e8b406d","goal_text":"Observe and compare plant parts and show care when investigating living plants.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Plant System (Plant Parts and Functions)"},{"id":"cef979d2-c7d5-436f-9b19-3e43541127fb","topic_id":"9b36f9dd-6e28-4c22-841e-7ec8bf7e2dd4","goal_text":"Identify the digestive, respiratory, circulatory, skeletal and muscular systems and their broad functions.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Human System (Digestive System)"},{"id":"2ac24ca9-a995-44a5-8f76-5d3f0f9335e8","topic_id":"9b36f9dd-6e28-4c22-841e-7ec8bf7e2dd4","goal_text":"Name the mouth, gullet, stomach, small intestine and large intestine.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Human System (Digestive System)"},{"id":"63bacab8-ea9c-4f20-bce9-738211e844d3","topic_id":"9b36f9dd-6e28-4c22-841e-7ec8bf7e2dd4","goal_text":"Describe how the mouth begins digestion and the gullet moves food to the stomach.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Human System (Digestive System)"},{"id":"d85eba37-99e3-4a05-bb3f-781d117ebab7","topic_id":"9b36f9dd-6e28-4c22-841e-7ec8bf7e2dd4","goal_text":"Describe the stomach and small intestine in breaking down and absorbing food.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Human System (Digestive System)"},{"id":"54595c3c-5c2f-4d44-b831-b65eb9f784b8","topic_id":"9b36f9dd-6e28-4c22-841e-7ec8bf7e2dd4","goal_text":"Explain how the large intestine absorbs water from remaining undigested material.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Human System (Digestive System)"},{"id":"6cf804b3-975d-43dd-b284-10de0ecffa4e","topic_id":"9b36f9dd-6e28-4c22-841e-7ec8bf7e2dd4","goal_text":"Trace the order of the main parts of the digestive system.","goal_order":6,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Human System (Digestive System)"},{"id":"2fb67f3f-318f-4ba6-b6f7-4572a1af01aa","topic_id":"1ed12e7b-d32e-442f-a517-66cfe0d16b76","goal_text":"Recognise that matter has mass and occupies space.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Cycles in Matter and Water (Matter)"},{"id":"b047412b-f2f5-4c87-80ff-8c12ea3b840b","topic_id":"1ed12e7b-d32e-442f-a517-66cfe0d16b76","goal_text":"Distinguish solids by fixed shape and fixed volume.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Cycles in Matter and Water (Matter)"},{"id":"57af713f-5cfd-4383-b674-54b24b5079e6","topic_id":"1ed12e7b-d32e-442f-a517-66cfe0d16b76","goal_text":"Distinguish liquids by fixed volume but changing shape.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Cycles in Matter and Water (Matter)"},{"id":"092ee0ac-f0e3-41ad-b943-9e77fe3266ee","topic_id":"1ed12e7b-d32e-442f-a517-66cfe0d16b76","goal_text":"Distinguish gases by no fixed shape or volume.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Cycles in Matter and Water (Matter)"},{"id":"37083ea8-9ab8-4652-a4e1-1c661dac6268","topic_id":"1ed12e7b-d32e-442f-a517-66cfe0d16b76","goal_text":"Measure or compare mass and volume using appropriate apparatus.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Cycles in Matter and Water (Matter)"},{"id":"29bebc9d-b67a-4c8d-835a-6129acaf5b26","topic_id":"ad3a0047-3d32-4da5-9906-c42514f2cb75","goal_text":"Explain that objects are seen because they give out light or reflect light into our eyes.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Energy Forms and Uses (Light)"},{"id":"85a73bce-0425-4b21-8481-e7cccecfaa37","topic_id":"ad3a0047-3d32-4da5-9906-c42514f2cb75","goal_text":"Identify common light sources and objects seen by reflected light.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Energy Forms and Uses (Light)"},{"id":"a4013126-4815-4a5d-b284-c9bdb25a27c0","topic_id":"ad3a0047-3d32-4da5-9906-c42514f2cb75","goal_text":"Recognise that light travels in straight lines.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Energy Forms and Uses (Light)"},{"id":"7e8dd07e-eed1-42f9-91d0-3739924738c4","topic_id":"ad3a0047-3d32-4da5-9906-c42514f2cb75","goal_text":"Explain why shadows form when light is partly or completely blocked.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Energy Forms and Uses (Light)"},{"id":"8a1a93fd-1798-4e33-bf0d-e63272c50a47","topic_id":"ad3a0047-3d32-4da5-9906-c42514f2cb75","goal_text":"Investigate how object shape, size, position and distances affect shadows.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Energy Forms and Uses (Light)"},{"id":"6cf8306b-2622-4bda-bf04-f5228b787e1f","topic_id":"54e227fd-ef12-47d4-8947-04e73d08978a","goal_text":"Identify common heat sources and recognise heat as a form of energy.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Energy Forms and Uses (Heat)"},{"id":"21f8107e-77b2-4b51-8695-1b725ad42872","topic_id":"54e227fd-ef12-47d4-8947-04e73d08978a","goal_text":"Explain temperature as a measure of how hot or cold an object is.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Energy Forms and Uses (Heat)"},{"id":"85632727-8455-41c6-9b4e-c0d1c0c4d494","topic_id":"54e227fd-ef12-47d4-8947-04e73d08978a","goal_text":"Distinguish heat from temperature and measure temperature with suitable tools.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Energy Forms and Uses (Heat)"},{"id":"8de7f348-812b-4664-8b3d-7cd072e7bd3a","topic_id":"54e227fd-ef12-47d4-8947-04e73d08978a","goal_text":"Explain how heat moves from hotter to colder regions until temperatures become equal.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Energy Forms and Uses (Heat)"},{"id":"7e89f59a-39cc-4adb-bd74-bffc4aadd888","topic_id":"54e227fd-ef12-47d4-8947-04e73d08978a","goal_text":"Relate an object's temperature change to gaining or losing heat.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Energy Forms and Uses (Heat)"},{"id":"e4cfce3e-7931-4104-8192-5ae9b9316c65","topic_id":"54e227fd-ef12-47d4-8947-04e73d08978a","goal_text":"Recognise expansion, contraction and changes of state caused by heat gain or loss.","goal_order":6,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Energy Forms and Uses (Heat)"},{"id":"490513ba-d9a7-48b4-95e5-d528179a55c9","topic_id":"54e227fd-ef12-47d4-8947-04e73d08978a","goal_text":"Compare good and poor conductors of heat using everyday examples.","goal_order":7,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P4 Energy Forms and Uses (Heat)"},{"id":"3bb3815c-8c6d-4eee-9817-24ae92efa296","topic_id":"7b3fdcb0-2c22-486b-b5f2-ae5814585cb4","goal_text":"Recognise cells as basic units of life and reproduction as a way living things continue their kind.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Cycles in Plants and Animals (Reproduction)"},{"id":"15123647-ef71-46d5-87c4-6e74cfa46283","topic_id":"7b3fdcb0-2c22-486b-b5f2-ae5814585cb4","goal_text":"Describe pollination and fertilisation in the sexual reproduction of flowering plants.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Cycles in Plants and Animals (Reproduction)"},{"id":"ff27e81a-4f62-4962-9b46-6617be19b338","topic_id":"7b3fdcb0-2c22-486b-b5f2-ae5814585cb4","goal_text":"Explain how seeds are dispersed and the conditions needed for germination.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Cycles in Plants and Animals (Reproduction)"},{"id":"94248ce1-556c-4fd0-92ac-597c2fddbbf3","topic_id":"7b3fdcb0-2c22-486b-b5f2-ae5814585cb4","goal_text":"Distinguish between plants that reproduce using seeds and those using spores.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Cycles in Plants and Animals (Reproduction)"},{"id":"a505da29-899a-4533-9f3b-84904a48ee46","topic_id":"7b3fdcb0-2c22-486b-b5f2-ae5814585cb4","goal_text":"Describe human fertilisation using sperm and egg and how a fertilised egg develops in the womb.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Cycles in Plants and Animals (Reproduction)"},{"id":"5a9737fd-f8fa-41f7-8392-a6daf1b9c072","topic_id":"7b3fdcb0-2c22-486b-b5f2-ae5814585cb4","goal_text":"Compare fertilisation in plants and humans while treating living things with respect.","goal_order":6,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Cycles in Plants and Animals (Reproduction)"},{"id":"7adeba5f-3797-4b8f-bd49-90ad84f66cac","topic_id":"a89b04b5-ce8e-4969-b9b8-ddeb13e1fd50","goal_text":"Identify water as a solid, liquid or gas and explain changes of state caused by heating or cooling.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Cycles in Matter and Water (Water)"},{"id":"534b6624-ae08-489e-ac6e-27db954f3e10","topic_id":"a89b04b5-ce8e-4969-b9b8-ddeb13e1fd50","goal_text":"Use 0°C as the melting/freezing point of pure water and 100°C as its boiling point at normal atmospheric pressure.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Cycles in Matter and Water (Water)"},{"id":"fcf4092b-094b-46d9-aede-4214962ceff3","topic_id":"a89b04b5-ce8e-4969-b9b8-ddeb13e1fd50","goal_text":"Distinguish evaporation from boiling and condensation from freezing.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Cycles in Matter and Water (Water)"},{"id":"8137468c-2d7b-49ab-95cd-7dfb7da8fd35","topic_id":"a89b04b5-ce8e-4969-b9b8-ddeb13e1fd50","goal_text":"Investigate how wind, temperature and exposed surface area affect evaporation.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Cycles in Matter and Water (Water)"},{"id":"e1d0cfb5-c977-41de-ae98-af2a65fb9d33","topic_id":"a89b04b5-ce8e-4969-b9b8-ddeb13e1fd50","goal_text":"Explain the roles of evaporation and condensation in the water cycle.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Cycles in Matter and Water (Water)"},{"id":"19d884b6-9cee-4430-a71f-353d932cf8ba","topic_id":"a89b04b5-ce8e-4969-b9b8-ddeb13e1fd50","goal_text":"Describe the importance of water for life and the effects of pollution.","goal_order":6,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Cycles in Matter and Water (Water)"},{"id":"0d57a7d2-0658-4e10-ab29-fb5dd2fb8654","topic_id":"a89b04b5-ce8e-4969-b9b8-ddeb13e1fd50","goal_text":"Suggest responsible ways to conserve usable water.","goal_order":7,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Cycles in Matter and Water (Water)"},{"id":"236cc249-16f2-4c80-94cd-c5c4e1c76dfd","topic_id":"2e484fcc-0d1c-4244-8aa3-097ae00880e5","goal_text":"Identify water-carrying tubes as parts of the plant transport system.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Plant System (Respiratory and Circulatory Systems)"},{"id":"46a93f3d-6b04-4792-a017-cfdddf5bee9b","topic_id":"2e484fcc-0d1c-4244-8aa3-097ae00880e5","goal_text":"Explain how water absorbed by roots moves to stems and leaves.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Plant System (Respiratory and Circulatory Systems)"},{"id":"b37e1494-cd76-408b-88a6-91ec78242fc8","topic_id":"2e484fcc-0d1c-4244-8aa3-097ae00880e5","goal_text":"Identify food-carrying tubes and explain how food made in leaves reaches other parts.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Plant System (Respiratory and Circulatory Systems)"},{"id":"645efa01-8bfd-4188-b4b8-aeb69eea1954","topic_id":"2e484fcc-0d1c-4244-8aa3-097ae00880e5","goal_text":"Use observations and simple demonstrations as evidence of transport in plants.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Plant System (Respiratory and Circulatory Systems)"},{"id":"480bb8f0-67d3-4e45-9584-1229720376b2","topic_id":"2e484fcc-0d1c-4244-8aa3-097ae00880e5","goal_text":"Compare the different jobs of water-carrying and food-carrying tubes without requiring specialist tube names.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Plant System (Respiratory and Circulatory Systems)"},{"id":"0a836023-ec8e-41f5-9376-9208e959e2ef","topic_id":"15acb72b-e0a1-41d0-a591-127e486aeaf4","goal_text":"Recognise that air contains nitrogen, oxygen, carbon dioxide and water vapour.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Human System (Respiratory and Circulatory Systems)"},{"id":"16b9890d-7fe8-4fb1-871a-75bf7b9a75d0","topic_id":"15acb72b-e0a1-41d0-a591-127e486aeaf4","goal_text":"Identify the nose, windpipe and lungs and describe their roles in breathing.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Human System (Respiratory and Circulatory Systems)"},{"id":"dd2d9732-25fb-4dec-8575-c51c6843d92e","topic_id":"15acb72b-e0a1-41d0-a591-127e486aeaf4","goal_text":"Identify the heart, blood and blood vessels and explain how substances move around the body.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Human System (Respiratory and Circulatory Systems)"},{"id":"f934adb7-5392-4981-8319-03b64d642d4f","topic_id":"15acb72b-e0a1-41d0-a591-127e486aeaf4","goal_text":"Explain how the digestive, respiratory and circulatory systems work together.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Human System (Respiratory and Circulatory Systems)"},{"id":"9974ca2f-9b72-48de-90ca-905f5547aaea","topic_id":"15acb72b-e0a1-41d0-a591-127e486aeaf4","goal_text":"Compare how plants, fish and humans take in oxygen and release carbon dioxide.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Human System (Respiratory and Circulatory Systems)"},{"id":"e4042b62-3ec3-4ab1-8ae6-ef500023da0d","topic_id":"15acb72b-e0a1-41d0-a591-127e486aeaf4","goal_text":"Compare transport of substances in human blood vessels with transport in plants.","goal_order":6,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Human System (Respiratory and Circulatory Systems)"},{"id":"00f8f75c-3568-4ea2-bf72-5f00951be02c","topic_id":"15acb72b-e0a1-41d0-a591-127e486aeaf4","goal_text":"Use simple observations to explain the role of these systems without advanced anatomical detail.","goal_order":7,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Human System (Respiratory and Circulatory Systems)"},{"id":"48b625fb-2e85-400d-a4ee-7b2cb877cf65","topic_id":"4410f03c-c504-47e1-9bb6-735336557447","goal_text":"Identify batteries, wires, bulbs and switches as parts of a simple electrical system.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Electrical System"},{"id":"e465f2ce-28ab-441f-8967-6b39cc353600","topic_id":"4410f03c-c504-47e1-9bb6-735336557447","goal_text":"Explain why a complete closed circuit is required for electric current to flow.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Electrical System"},{"id":"4f1827a4-779f-4358-b5df-d977be28227c","topic_id":"4410f03c-c504-47e1-9bb6-735336557447","goal_text":"Identify electrical conductors and insulators using appropriate circuit tests.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Electrical System"},{"id":"651fae24-f987-4954-9d87-570972d4807e","topic_id":"4410f03c-c504-47e1-9bb6-735336557447","goal_text":"Read and construct simple circuits from diagrams.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Electrical System"},{"id":"6459c0fe-c118-4325-ae5a-6c43339f25a7","topic_id":"4410f03c-c504-47e1-9bb6-735336557447","goal_text":"Investigate how the number of batteries connected in series affects bulb brightness.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Electrical System"},{"id":"bac2650a-4c5e-4755-8abb-36ae7fd8b883","topic_id":"4410f03c-c504-47e1-9bb6-735336557447","goal_text":"Compare bulbs arranged in series and parallel circuits.","goal_order":6,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Electrical System"},{"id":"f3eb8ab0-b723-4156-a0f7-731796107d7f","topic_id":"4410f03c-c504-47e1-9bb6-735336557447","goal_text":"Practise safe electricity use and conservation.","goal_order":7,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P5 Electrical System"},{"id":"68196d7b-7e2b-47ca-b1d6-24ef5f22248c","topic_id":"12690174-9480-42a7-b8d4-f08135cf133f","goal_text":"Identify the Sun as the primary source of light and heat energy for Earth.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Energy Forms and Uses (Photosynthesis)"},{"id":"8337e731-6f0b-4cb9-9168-d202d2f2cf6c","topic_id":"12690174-9480-42a7-b8d4-f08135cf133f","goal_text":"Explain that green plants use light energy, carbon dioxide and water to make sugar and oxygen during photosynthesis.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Energy Forms and Uses (Photosynthesis)"},{"id":"fdd0ffb4-9f4a-423a-a4f1-bbe0796979c1","topic_id":"12690174-9480-42a7-b8d4-f08135cf133f","goal_text":"Distinguish how green plants and animals obtain food and energy.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Energy Forms and Uses (Photosynthesis)"},{"id":"32801666-e29a-4331-bd96-7baa5e507678","topic_id":"12690174-9480-42a7-b8d4-f08135cf133f","goal_text":"Recognise that respiration releases energy from food in both plants and animals.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Energy Forms and Uses (Photosynthesis)"},{"id":"733300e6-5900-45d9-b5a9-2d563333a19d","topic_id":"12690174-9480-42a7-b8d4-f08135cf133f","goal_text":"Investigate photosynthesis by changing one requirement at a time and observing evidence.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Energy Forms and Uses (Photosynthesis)"},{"id":"510e01ed-6d84-4e06-8d55-a5a34817347b","topic_id":"12690174-9480-42a7-b8d4-f08135cf133f","goal_text":"Use observations to make justified conclusions about photosynthesis and plant survival.","goal_order":6,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Energy Forms and Uses (Photosynthesis)"},{"id":"f9ca7389-194d-4d77-9ea9-d50875cfb114","topic_id":"80771895-1e32-40dc-9302-64f48d609df9","goal_text":"Recognise kinetic, potential, light, electrical, sound and heat energy in familiar situations.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Energy Conversion"},{"id":"391f1b2c-9a5d-4722-8768-4e70e942b73e","topic_id":"80771895-1e32-40dc-9302-64f48d609df9","goal_text":"Identify kinetic energy in moving objects and potential energy in stored situations.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Energy Conversion"},{"id":"cfc05a70-f4be-45a7-90fa-9868380c46fa","topic_id":"80771895-1e32-40dc-9302-64f48d609df9","goal_text":"Trace energy conversions in bulbs, fans, bells and other familiar devices.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Energy Conversion"},{"id":"1ccebe87-ee3d-4c62-a232-16d9e434e714","topic_id":"80771895-1e32-40dc-9302-64f48d609df9","goal_text":"Explain useful energy outputs and unwanted heat or sound outputs.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Energy Conversion"},{"id":"27797b8b-c350-4ef3-a699-690f97a625ba","topic_id":"80771895-1e32-40dc-9302-64f48d609df9","goal_text":"Connect food energy and sunlight to simple energy-conversion pathways.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Energy Conversion"},{"id":"e2b0639d-2e69-4149-b677-9b7060d3952a","topic_id":"80771895-1e32-40dc-9302-64f48d609df9","goal_text":"Recognise that much of the energy people use is ultimately derived from the Sun.","goal_order":6,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Energy Conversion"},{"id":"06dc7fd3-84dd-43f0-9a31-494e286cc1d6","topic_id":"80771895-1e32-40dc-9302-64f48d609df9","goal_text":"Suggest responsible ways to conserve energy in everyday life.","goal_order":7,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Energy Conversion"},{"id":"818ea617-ce48-4c25-8a0e-244dee7c94c3","topic_id":"78cdc285-1e39-417d-a272-fa933236406a","goal_text":"Identify a force as a push or a pull and describe how forces affect motion or shape.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Interaction of Forces (Frictional Force, Gravitational Force, Elastic Spring Force)"},{"id":"69dde461-530b-45de-b805-07b160032e6e","topic_id":"78cdc285-1e39-417d-a272-fa933236406a","goal_text":"Recognise magnetic, gravitational, frictional and elastic spring forces in daily life.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Interaction of Forces (Frictional Force, Gravitational Force, Elastic Spring Force)"},{"id":"c07fea6c-7db2-4986-b818-a43af97c1256","topic_id":"78cdc285-1e39-417d-a272-fa933236406a","goal_text":"Explain that gravitational force gives objects weight and pulls them towards Earth.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Interaction of Forces (Frictional Force, Gravitational Force, Elastic Spring Force)"},{"id":"d664bb48-4397-4663-adce-4b9ae74d2539","topic_id":"78cdc285-1e39-417d-a272-fa933236406a","goal_text":"Describe how friction affects sliding objects and how surface properties affect friction.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Interaction of Forces (Frictional Force, Gravitational Force, Elastic Spring Force)"},{"id":"2701f565-3354-41e1-9b94-61e5e171127e","topic_id":"78cdc285-1e39-417d-a272-fa933236406a","goal_text":"Investigate the effect of friction by controlling variables in a fair test.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Interaction of Forces (Frictional Force, Gravitational Force, Elastic Spring Force)"},{"id":"25db3638-0651-43ba-aa09-f8b4aa7aee0c","topic_id":"78cdc285-1e39-417d-a272-fa933236406a","goal_text":"Explain what happens when a spring is stretched or compressed and released.","goal_order":6,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Interaction of Forces (Frictional Force, Gravitational Force, Elastic Spring Force)"},{"id":"f4e50764-771a-48f0-a39a-ffaa64fee1e9","topic_id":"78cdc285-1e39-417d-a272-fa933236406a","goal_text":"Investigate spring force using careful measurements and evidence.","goal_order":7,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Interaction of Forces (Frictional Force, Gravitational Force, Elastic Spring Force)"},{"id":"4689686b-f367-4b52-823e-056bcbd8c985","topic_id":"98d9e935-01d8-4458-bb66-f775d3eef90b","goal_text":"Identify the effects of light, water, temperature and food availability on survival.","goal_order":1,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Interactions within the Environment"},{"id":"bcecf641-2e1a-42e5-8bda-b46afe8e67ae","topic_id":"98d9e935-01d8-4458-bb66-f775d3eef90b","goal_text":"Explain the roles of producers, consumers and decomposers in the environment.","goal_order":2,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Interactions within the Environment"},{"id":"381f3ae4-4ded-4a11-8a11-82cc0d0a9602","topic_id":"98d9e935-01d8-4458-bb66-f775d3eef90b","goal_text":"Trace energy from the Sun through food chains and food webs, including predators and prey.","goal_order":3,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Interactions within the Environment"},{"id":"ba74af6d-b974-45ce-bc09-5bb53a82919d","topic_id":"98d9e935-01d8-4458-bb66-f775d3eef90b","goal_text":"Differentiate organisms, populations and communities.","goal_order":4,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Interactions within the Environment"},{"id":"7aca05a2-1086-4a62-bbb7-08abcda59898","topic_id":"98d9e935-01d8-4458-bb66-f775d3eef90b","goal_text":"Compare the communities supported by different habitats.","goal_order":5,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Interactions within the Environment"},{"id":"905718c1-6832-4586-b723-1bfa844f43e4","topic_id":"98d9e935-01d8-4458-bb66-f775d3eef90b","goal_text":"Explain how organisms respond when conditions become unfavourable.","goal_order":6,"syllabus_reference":"2023 Primary Science Syllabus - P6 Standard - Interactions within the Environme