n_id":"109777b5-07f1-4189-84a1-25b704258b6a"},{"explanation":"25/100 × 200 = 50.","question_id":"34b38c8c-6b1e-4c15-a64f-2c974332d1df","correct_option_id":"911181dc-1009-4a5e-b4dc-d70a4b23fa40"},{"explanation":"12 ÷ 30 × 100% = 40%.","question_id":"1736bb53-dae7-4b84-bacf-f85ef1f1df8f","correct_option_id":"f0568594-e4a5-4c6b-a5d1-34bf48f05390"},{"explanation":"10% of 60 is 6 and 5% is 3, so total is 9.","question_id":"4079529c-669e-4692-b7d7-55f601d100d4","correct_option_id":"3df2571a-5218-4c57-9ec0-c38fa80b8693"},{"explanation":"25% × $80 = $20.","question_id":"15aa8094-bce1-44d9-8871-2b52c72f5362","correct_option_id":"95e88a60-8e9b-4574-bf91-26a8f2f3a9a1"},{"explanation":"9% of $40 is $3.60. Add to $40 to get $43.60.","question_id":"ad39cb15-569d-46c7-82f8-24156420a1b0","correct_option_id":"3c386f99-d694-431d-a032-9153196d7102"},{"explanation":"4/100 × $500 = $20.","question_id":"34bde7d2-21f1-4b08-92ab-ffaa62657bb2","correct_option_id":"3991f961-3aa0-45da-81f8-75dacdd10385"},{"explanation":"8/32 = 1/4 = 25%.","question_id":"ab6b8fdf-30ab-41a5-b701-7d3df8aeb036","correct_option_id":"0fc9994b-658c-4b0b-be32-b0bf36681f86"},{"explanation":"10% of $120 is $12; $120 − $12 = $108.","question_id":"28d9f424-b66e-4442-9399-1c34fe2226fb","correct_option_id":"5b74e130-eaa5-4a7c-82be-7cbf705f5967"},{"explanation":"35/100 × 240 = 84 books.","question_id":"21239653-a53f-4ff7-9675-6ae7598ff59b","correct_option_id":"f2c87592-02c3-4dff-9d0b-2e2ff0862f73"},{"explanation":"Discounted price is $200 − $20 = $180. GST is 8% × $180 = $14.40, so final price is $194.40.","question_id":"6054b2a8-f5e4-4b02-85a3-5bb29cba7693","correct_option_id":"367f2d9d-c4c2-4722-97c5-c2f777b88203"},{"explanation":"The unit rate is 7 litres for every one minute.","question_id":"ce8f5266-1363-4fbb-892a-55520ce31978","correct_option_id":"29d38f66-2998-4d5e-9572-9dc938e199f4"},{"explanation":"36 ÷ 6 = 6 pages per minute.","question_id":"962f0187-0cbf-420f-b721-c00d5b21d9df","correct_option_id":"cae048b8-29bb-47bd-8142-a2d9d122e13a"},{"explanation":"8 × $5 = $40.","question_id":"74a49c2a-df40-4e1a-864c-2b012f0574b6","correct_option_id":"b784f5e9-c6fb-4bb4-80e4-22531661d8ac"},{"explanation":"28 ÷ 4 = 7 minutes.","question_id":"d4f5b7c8-695d-484f-9d5e-2434288b324f","correct_option_id":"a53b8c6c-ca06-4870-b470-de0224f27009"},{"explanation":"30 ÷ 5 = 6 km per hour.","question_id":"e1a8dcd0-294d-47cd-95ca-92b4a4d18128","correct_option_id":"2a6d353b-4e31-4036-937c-b03e0205f369"},{"explanation":"12 × 4 = 48 buns.","question_id":"d3ca21df-b688-49de-b861-4d7a604631e3","correct_option_id":"a78cb7bb-bc14-4444-88fa-e730e4667457"},{"explanation":"A rate of filling compares volume with time, such as ml/min.","question_id":"471502f8-8486-4abf-a866-88a9814a9222","correct_option_id":"481e4eec-c80d-43da-9467-bc1a0fe9b595"},{"explanation":"72 ÷ 3 = 24 km/h.","question_id":"e72d75b4-585f-4dc1-9334-d429c8454a5a","correct_option_id":"2b63a4ce-8c3c-4052-a39d-a893f05ea289"},{"explanation":"63 ÷ 9 = 7 minutes.","question_id":"9172244b-4375-4c4d-b71e-5aefa1738209","correct_option_id":"8b6c82d9-c73c-4a2d-b2c4-c688766354eb"},{"explanation":"$15 ÷ 6 = $2.50 per drink.","question_id":"a1eb01e4-a0fc-4e1a-803b-c70715bf506a","correct_option_id":"657e3898-0fb4-453d-a526-56fe477c17ee"},{"explanation":"18 × 5 = 90 cartons.","question_id":"f526a72e-ff10-4838-a808-5b223acf8883","correct_option_id":"06f3da22-02be-4f0b-be73-1be7255a2fe7"},{"explanation":"The rate is 180 ÷ 3 = 60 ml/s. In 25 seconds, 60 × 25 = 1,500 ml.","question_id":"bda2d24d-5474-4ee8-a81d-a8cd5f97c1e3","correct_option_id":"ae62a5aa-abcf-4703-8b99-c162ed698670"},{"explanation":"Area = 1/2 × 10 × 6 = 30 cm².","question_id":"716172bf-d686-4591-9b9e-36c89e7f1e67","correct_option_id":"eccd0fc7-f765-46a3-9d96-b7e5fd8a6a61"},{"explanation":"The height must make a right angle with the base or its extension.","question_id":"00a13d36-54e8-424d-89f7-f0c6bbb3ff86","correct_option_id":"ac6bc883-6a1a-4862-8f54-883e68ada385"},{"explanation":"1/2 × 8 × 5 = 20 m².","question_id":"04a46f0c-2c71-4bb9-b63c-a8c70c78860e","correct_option_id":"5c7aa515-8104-4674-807f-6154a4ce17fa"},{"explanation":"Each area = 1/2 × 12 × 7 = 42 cm².","question_id":"6bfec546-8e27-4fbb-8f4d-e0bc60642fda","correct_option_id":"20efd81a-4d7a-4a43-9b2a-28a4ab2e5d78"},{"explanation":"24 = 1/2 × 8 × height, so height = 24 × 2 ÷ 8 = 6 cm.","question_id":"24045a99-68b6-4d3a-89da-f8332e82915e","correct_option_id":"a406a7ae-1f49-43d6-bf79-9ce6fc02a4fe"},{"explanation":"Rectangle: 20 cm²; triangle: 6 cm²; total: 26 cm².","question_id":"922bc0a3-6206-4c6c-af5a-f6ef31171797","correct_option_id":"0796302c-194d-48b6-86e5-0d263f88a646"},{"explanation":"1/2 × 15 × 4 = 30 cm².","question_id":"7554f5a0-bcf2-4957-a290-faf81d0e1f53","correct_option_id":"2cc52998-9d4b-4e44-8dd1-0f0e3e408075"},{"explanation":"Use the perpendicular height 6 cm, not the unrelated sloping side.","question_id":"5e9d06e9-a1b3-49dd-98c8-19865b550866","correct_option_id":"45e1e6a9-9ceb-4010-bcd3-1522f9408738"},{"explanation":"Square: 7 × 7 = 49 cm². Triangle: 1/2 × 6 × 4 = 12 cm². Total: 61 cm².","question_id":"29a2ccf9-00d6-4488-9dd0-9d6b79d2493f","correct_option_id":"3b882154-eeec-49fc-9a85-065f13ba28f7"},{"explanation":"1/2 × 14 × 9 = 63 cm².","question_id":"b08cab0d-2cbf-439d-ad4f-b53e2d8e94bd","correct_option_id":"8a0093e4-c242-4bce-b3f5-d517554180db"},{"explanation":"Rectangle area 60 cm² minus triangle area 12 cm² equals 48 cm².","question_id":"1a9cce19-aa73-4d03-8a85-9f4751cd1215","correct_option_id":"1397de79-e0b7-4f61-a688-d53437967f00"},{"explanation":"Square: 64 m²; triangle: 30 m²; total: 94 m².","question_id":"e7ec8343-5dfe-4d15-bd74-916e82f988bd","correct_option_id":"ec1d3d9b-6d1d-4e7e-80f0-a865dfc03b12"},{"explanation":"3 × 8 = 24 unit cubes.","question_id":"47fef859-a63a-42ca-bd38-a3270308f660","correct_option_id":"77dba2ad-16e3-4f2c-b33a-2fd67922a04d"},{"explanation":"Cubic centimetres (cm³) measure three-dimensional volume.","question_id":"8194cbbd-e320-40fe-8411-52476d9a7f21","correct_option_id":"2969d002-27c7-4311-b437-27d5dac83113"},{"explanation":"5 × 4 × 3 = 60 cm³.","question_id":"aab645aa-e0ee-445d-9079-1e5c9baf93b3","correct_option_id":"9540015b-5631-4ab9-b12d-b07edd98724a"},{"explanation":"4 × 4 × 4 = 64 cm³.","question_id":"2e11cfe1-9562-40a9-9ce2-9cc9a06155e1","correct_option_id":"0d93693d-28e7-461d-b86d-0c7400004b0f"},{"explanation":"10 × 8 × 5 = 400 cm³.","question_id":"f82b1506-3523-48d9-a989-407e2ede0dc6","correct_option_id":"367d056e-2c50-4ca1-8e07-045e3685a3d1"},{"explanation":"1 cm³ = 1 ml, so 1,250 cm³ = 1,250 ml.","question_id":"ed632fb6-aee6-47c1-a9fc-849bca9180c0","correct_option_id":"cd75bd3f-566e-47de-9864-c078a7ca0d43"},{"explanation":"3,000 ÷ 1,000 = 3 litres.","question_id":"053bc746-dc41-4946-ae2d-c52c878563d1","correct_option_id":"d3cdf0c9-3c9e-4303-a695-cbee856116ec"},{"explanation":"An isometric grid helps show three-dimensional cubes and cuboids in a two-dimensional drawing.","question_id":"c255c62e-fbb5-4b9f-b540-52af9ba3b070","correct_option_id":"312fef59-706f-47ef-9977-4768f3e6046c"},{"explanation":"12 × 5 × 2 = 120 cm³.","question_id":"f2dfabf3-cad3-4647-8ed0-3ec0fb2cb5c1","correct_option_id":"482c2d58-f606-430f-979c-1b26084d9c91"},{"explanation":"15 × 10 × 12 = 1,800 cm³ = 1,800 ml = 1.8 l.","question_id":"6ee09745-5082-46dc-92eb-210940f98f8b","correct_option_id":"f57c59e4-5f26-40a8-9c81-e01e2ca1fc12"},{"explanation":"6 litres = 6,000 cm³. Base area = 20 × 15 = 300 cm². Depth = 6,000 ÷ 300 = 20 cm.","question_id":"d2b082f6-a1ac-415f-a4fc-7f6532a62e61","correct_option_id":"9f8873e3-4829-4fb5-80bc-761a657b6445"},{"explanation":"First volume 120 cm³; second volume 60 cm³. Combined = 180 cm³.","question_id":"4ba02fe0-6a44-4364-bc6e-591ece4bf14d","correct_option_id":"302d4d3a-06ae-4a59-96da-00ed31e04cac"},{"explanation":"180° − 65° = 115°.","question_id":"c95811eb-60dd-47c6-947c-f2befbb2ef27","correct_option_id":"0eb131dc-e44c-43bd-b5e8-94217e43e5ca"},{"explanation":"A full turn around a point is 360°.","question_id":"71265c76-62dc-4431-990e-a8de64fb5c90","correct_option_id":"68fd0b7b-38f4-48d9-94fc-626f63a900ad"},{"explanation":"Vertically opposite angles are equal.","question_id":"ace52c32-2ce2-4ae6-9115-c9bd6d0fa19a","correct_option_id":"5b9dfb15-00e2-4dfc-8281-8a5cce9de6d8"},{"explanation":"180° − 124° = 56°.","question_id":"530599f0-8662-4ffa-a6b4-bb679a6e4332","correct_option_id":"85071549-2790-4784-b560-c1a245782566"},{"explanation":"360° − (90° + 120° + 70°) = 80°.","question_id":"6c6f420f-21e2-436b-924c-ec78b25c1c21","correct_option_id":"d52672c7-9ecc-4ef8-8c25-ccb8e2e9a601"},{"explanation":"Adjacent straight-line angles total 180°, so 180° − 130° = 50°.","question_id":"8f491187-002b-4ef8-95ac-c6a9da68005c","correct_option_id":"54478dc2-9e31-4652-8e7e-898b7cf03511"},{"explanation":"The vertically opposite angle equals 35°.","question_id":"c1c2f492-7a7c-4ccb-831c-0535b02159d6","correct_option_id":"c29cff08-c215-490a-9849-9866354cfdd6"},{"explanation":"360° − 275° = 85°.","question_id":"9f6d33e6-2114-43d8-827d-df9cc1c3be11","correct_option_id":"bfa152a6-dece-472c-8e07-1cda307eec23"},{"explanation":"Three equal parts share 180°, so each angle is 180° ÷ 3 = 60°.","question_id":"da8f732b-e9df-479d-bd08-80bfa953b054","correct_option_id":"0c41304f-82d9-4d92-9a83-8c46b07ef5d0"},{"explanation":"Each adjacent angle is 65°, so their sum is 130°.","question_id":"24ffdfb5-86bc-45c7-9b24-25d3aee852b6","correct_option_id":"67cdd54d-be16-4428-b12e-326fc3a156ed"},{"explanation":"360° − (60° + 60° + 90°) = 150°.","question_id":"54c615df-711f-4a6d-9bb0-611276726d39","correct_option_id":"96891d48-3cfa-4106-ae8d-2770094821e1"},{"explanation":"Adjacent angles on the straight line add to 180°: 180° − 140° = 40°.","question_id":"9a900dc0-3736-4930-8dcd-92fe6ce9f40d","correct_option_id":"7f04521f-e908-4529-8d63-1cb613a08307"},{"explanation":"180° − 45° − 65° = 70°.","question_id":"9b844076-bd8b-4d15-8c61-4f621f3a52c3","correct_option_id":"b9615baf-3f46-4449-aaeb-1561fc815f99"},{"explanation":"180° ÷ 3 = 60°.","question_id":"c7762ddc-f8a9-4f77-97e6-453793259060","correct_option_id":"0785a161-9fa5-43e3-803d-675d17d6c891"},{"explanation":"180° − 50° − 50° = 80°.","question_id":"f5b5be52-be69-402a-b50b-bacd854fc5c1","correct_option_id":"0af11ef3-87c2-4f0b-8cb2-e2a3104a49f1"},{"explanation":"90° − 34° = 56°.","question_id":"1ca22aee-66fe-4d82-b2de-1d1174a28d37","correct_option_id":"dc872dd8-72c6-4ab1-8891-6df78c79734e"},{"explanation":"In an isosceles triangle, equal sides face equal angles.","question_id":"40267201-5ba5-421e-a2a7-13b7b1354d6f","correct_option_id":"1e7124a4-fde5-43fc-9b0c-eba2f11a5406"},{"explanation":"180° − 38° − 72° = 70°.","question_id":"b68cf7ff-dfee-4b5f-8cf0-867fa552daf8","correct_option_id":"4ab98da5-43f3-4812-9f23-688c1f3427bd"},{"explanation":"90° − 62° = 28°.","question_id":"45ceec28-18dd-45f7-a2c2-bfec216d1910","correct_option_id":"f88f1a96-a6ce-4796-85cc-d9ec65086af4"},{"explanation":"An equilateral triangle has three equal sides.","question_id":"073fd3eb-1bd8-43e0-a8da-75987afb2cbb","correct_option_id":"55c49082-1c13-4332-bfc6-62b0fb189336"},{"explanation":"The remaining 140° is divided equally: 140° ÷ 2 = 70°.","question_id":"4f53dcc2-47c5-4dca-9712-8b70d7722f55","correct_option_id":"312e00a8-847f-41e6-957e-e7baafd569b2"},{"explanation":"55° + 95° = 150°, so the remaining angle is 30°.","question_id":"0455872b-d4d5-4981-971f-f1a1a52a8e6f","correct_option_id":"879c4875-c033-43b0-a96d-ae04861ee712"},{"explanation":"(180° − 72°) ÷ 2 = 54°.","question_id":"7cc7fe06-2153-4ddd-b901-d47d7a417cce","correct_option_id":"ae9dc0a5-1cd7-4c01-b91f-fa295408f031"},{"explanation":"The other acute angle is 90° − 36° = 54°, which is larger than 36°.","question_id":"ebdd06de-5ab8-4bde-93ba-e95176202957","correct_option_id":"997f8f89-2f0b-4fe8-b62e-7a14e8fb6f67"},{"explanation":"Opposite angles in a parallelogram are equal.","question_id":"592867a5-41fe-4293-89c8-440054d38d69","correct_option_id":"00e31bf0-9262-4faf-a686-ae80c672185d"},{"explanation":"Adjacent angles add to 180°: 180° − 115° = 65°.","question_id":"a582b06a-826a-4b38-b9d9-0c81ea47f314","correct_option_id":"0c505013-7596-458b-8924-3588a65874f7"},{"explanation":"All four sides of a rhombus are equal.","question_id":"25956290-0a64-42db-ba92-2fdde1d69ac9","correct_option_id":"c90abdbd-bff1-4a2c-b317-b1624513c76e"},{"explanation":"Angles on the same leg between parallel sides add to 180°, so 180° − 72° = 108°.","question_id":"9d398f7d-ab98-4c78-9040-de54428d7c64","correct_option_id":"008643f7-fe62-428f-af0d-04ebb2b67e1a"},{"explanation":"180° − 100° = 80°.","question_id":"ee95a13c-fe74-421a-9ff5-a9ae3e19e9da","correct_option_id":"9aff24f4-cfea-451c-9f75-24f55b6560ee"},{"explanation":"A quadrilateral can be split into two triangles, each of 180°.","question_id":"762c4886-bf0b-4e02-9a2f-ee37b6d776ee","correct_option_id":"f51fec47-6fd5-455b-83f5-32c4dbb45906"},{"explanation":"In every parallelogram, both pairs of opposite sides are parallel.","question_id":"3fa2aced-6bb4-4f92-b923-eb2f293c3b5d","correct_option_id":"5109823c-e964-40e0-9fd7-d0bcaccd93c9"},{"explanation":"Opposite rhombus angles are equal.","question_id":"6ceb6a15-ae28-410b-aa70-4748f8760ddf","correct_option_id":"21341bbe-e62e-4eba-8a87-df44890d6e75"},{"explanation":"Consecutive interior angles on the leg sum to 180°, so x = 55°.","question_id":"72590a8a-68ec-4592-88d0-3ee2b6b13d0c","correct_option_id":"cf0da873-ba70-4404-89fb-5ca24de37028"},{"explanation":"Neighbouring angles are supplementary: 180° − 73° = 107°.","question_id":"2144c176-081c-4fac-86e1-a5182818e403","correct_option_id":"f71b3022-b594-46c1-9170-bb5eaa261e40"},{"explanation":"The two remaining equal angles sum to 360° − 240° = 120°, so each is 60°.","question_id":"5704bf5f-4444-463f-9995-e01214e0a138","correct_option_id":"379f11ae-9034-4cf5-9eeb-711a36f20759"},{"explanation":"Each non-parallel leg connects supplementary angles: 180° − 68° = 112°, and 180° − 92° = 88°.","question_id":"9569075e-da39-4aa6-94db-5d3656b13270","correct_option_id":"7d41f3e9-8585-44a9-b530-06d41ef6267c"},{"explanation":"Divide by 2: (1/2) × (1/2) = 1/4.","question_id":"5923943b-9f25-427b-82a3-1418dc1714f7","correct_option_id":"4ddf2aed-b854-4b5b-9115-baf305468c38"},{"explanation":"Divide by 3: (3/4) × (1/3) = 1/4.","question_id":"9de1f8a7-2891-47b2-abb5-7e5670c54b9e","correct_option_id":"2333c34d-c7d7-403f-adc4-acf50eeffab5"},{"explanation":"Divide by 2: (2/3) × (1/2) = 1/3.","question_id":"99685aac-45f0-4565-a52a-79a28910e319","correct_option_id":"f41c29f2-49d1-4212-a3db-bea42b2a1030"},{"explanation":"Divide by 5: (5/6) × (1/5) = 1/6.","question_id":"0faf0d10-ad4a-4391-9910-f0e3ed05b684","correct_option_id":"c7557669-67f3-4aec-8ff3-afee6e0897c5"},{"explanation":"2 ÷ 2/3 = 2 × 3/2 = 3.","question_id":"a503d41c-f2f3-46cf-ae13-276242cbcd1e","correct_option_id":"b976d1b9-4ec9-440e-b705-befe3c1bc77c"},{"explanation":"2 ÷ 3/4 = 2 × 4/3 = 8/3.","question_id":"cf582bb4-119d-45bc-aad8-73411875c81a","correct_option_id":"93fb64fa-766f-43c3-896a-da9eb0d9fb35"},{"explanation":"2 ÷ 1/5 = 2 × 5/1 = 10.","question_id":"d599269b-b1fa-470a-a294-982554422b3e","correct_option_id":"a6cecf9c-e36c-45c0-ba53-0799ab73a907"},{"explanation":"2 ÷ 5/6 = 2 × 6/5 = 12/5.","question_id":"340a93a5-0f87-49cf-9797-c118f25fda34","correct_option_id":"426660a1-2a4e-4976-9a84-153377fa01d2"},{"explanation":"Total length ÷ piece length = 3/4 ÷ 1/8 = 6.","question_id":"acf01d89-98d7-4cc9-8c09-10f205d23bba","correct_option_id":"a6181087-d4b4-486c-8b1e-c4e1823de7f7"},{"explanation":"Total length ÷ piece length = 2/3 ÷ 1/6 = 4.","question_id":"63579a36-93c8-421b-b3ee-59986f0aec37","correct_option_id":"1a36f40f-a5a7-4a9e-a1e0-a84ea4c3a95c"},{"explanation":"Total length ÷ piece length = 3/5 ÷ 1/10 = 6.","question_id":"feabd539-e620-41ec-bcf6-c33dc474b2a2","correct_option_id":"f34d4208-ae26-4af8-a309-08e4b1e1765e"},{"explanation":"Total length ÷ piece length = 5/6 ÷ 1/3 = 5/2.","question_id":"54d90fe3-b675-4924-9cec-9764897ec990","corre